    "@value": "1933"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/okies/timeline/3",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "The migration to California begins in earnest; that summer economist Paul Taylor reports on white migrant families in the farm districts.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:gYear",
    "@value": "1935"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/okies/timeline/4",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "Los Angeles police post a border patrol, the \"bum blockade\", to turn back poor arrivals; it is withdrawn under threat of lawsuits.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:gYear",
    "@value": "1936"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/okies/timeline/5",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "Migration peaks in 1937 and 1938; up to 37,000 migrants reach Arizona's cotton fields.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:gYear",
    "@value": "1937"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/okies/timeline/6",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "John Steinbeck's The Grapes of Wrath and Carey McWilliams's Factories in the Field are published; county prosecutors charge more than two dozen people under the Indigent Act.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:gYear",
    "@value": "1939"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/okies/timeline/7",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "Fred Edwards drives from California to Spur, Texas, to bring back his brother-in-law Frank Duncan, and is later convicted.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:gYearMonth",
    "@value": "1939-12"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/okies/timeline/8",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "In Edwards v. California the Supreme Court strikes down the law, holding that states cannot bar poor migrants from other states.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:date",
