    "@type": "xsd:date",
    "@value": "1849-03-23"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/underground-railroad/timeline/6",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "The Fugitive Slave Act of 1850 is approved, commanding bystanders to help catch freedom seekers and penalizing anyone who aids them.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:date",
    "@value": "1850-09-18"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/underground-railroad/timeline/7",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "At Christiana, Pennsylvania, Black residents resist a Maryland slaveholder's attempt to recapture freedom seekers; the slaveholder is killed.",
