   "skos:definition": "A Tennessee lawyer, planter, enslaver and general (1767–1845) who won the Battle of New Orleans, led campaigns that took Creek and Seminole lands, and as the seventh president of the United States (1829–1837) vetoed the recharter of the Second Bank, faced down South Carolina's nullification of the tariff and drove the removal of Native nations west of the Mississippi.",
