   "skos:definition": "The federal immigration station on Angel Island in San Francisco Bay that from 1910 to 1940 inspected, interrogated and often detained arrivals from across the Pacific — above all Chinese immigrants under the Chinese exclusion laws — and is now a National Historic Landmark known for the poems detainees carved into its barrack walls.",
