   "skos:definition": "A naval battle of the American Revolutionary War fought on September 5, 1781, off the mouth of Chesapeake Bay between a French fleet under the comte de Grasse and a British fleet under Thomas Graves; though the fighting itself was brief and inconclusive, it left France in control of the bay, trapped Cornwallis's army at Yorktown and made the allied victory there possible.",
   "skos:inScheme": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/colonial-and-revolutionary"
   },
   "skos:prefLabel": "Battle of the Virginia Capes",
