   "skos:definition": "A Boston-born Philadelphia printer, writer, scientist and civic organizer (1706–1790) who became a colonial agent in London, a member of the Continental Congress, the first American minister received by a foreign government, a delegate to the Constitutional Convention and, after decades of owning enslaved people, president of Pennsylvania's antislavery society.",
