   "skos:definition": "The thirty-first U.S. state (admitted September 9, 1850) and the most populous since 1962, on the Pacific coast; homeland of many Native Californian peoples, then a Spanish and Mexican province, it was taken by the United States in the U.S.–Mexican War and admitted as a free state amid the Gold Rush, while its first legislature legalized the indenture of Native people.",
