   },
   "skos:definition": "The largest estuary in the United States, a drowned river valley about 190 miles long between Maryland and Virginia whose 64,000-square-mile watershed reaches into six states and the District of Columbia; homeland of Algonquian-speaking and other Native nations, the setting of English colonization, slavery's tobacco economy and decisive battles of two wars, and the object of a decades-long federal–state cleanup.",
