   "skos:definition": "Illinois's largest city and the third-largest in the United States (2020 census), built on Neshnabé (Potawatomi, Odawa and Ojibwe) land at the portage between the Great Lakes and the Mississippi watershed; incorporated in 1837, it became the nation's railroad, grain and meatpacking hub, rebuilt after the 1871 fire, and was a major destination of the Great Migration.",
