   "skos:definition": "Americans of Chinese descent, from the gold-rush and railroad workers of the 1850s and 1860s through the families who endured six decades of exclusion to the large, diverse post-1965 community; the 2020 census counted about 5.2 million people who identified as Chinese (except Taiwanese) alone or in any combination, the largest Asian group by that measure.",
