   },
   "skos:definition": "The federal law approved on May 6, 1882, that suspended the immigration of Chinese laborers for ten years and barred Chinese immigrants from naturalized citizenship — the first major U.S. law to restrict immigration by race and class, later extended, made permanent in 1902 and repealed only in 1943.",
