   },
   "skos:definition": "The period of U.S. history from roughly 1870 to 1900, named after Mark Twain and Charles Dudley Warner's 1873 satire, when railroads, factories, cities and immigration grew at unprecedented speed while wealth concentrated, labor conflict sharpened, and Black, Native, Chinese and working-class Americans faced disfranchisement, dispossession and exclusion.",
