   "skos:definition": "The longest and deepest economic downturn in U.S. history, which began in August 1929, hit bottom in March 1933 and lasted until wartime demand restored full employment in 1941, throwing about a quarter of the labor force out of work, collapsing the banking system and reshaping the federal government's role through the New Deal.",
