   },
   "skos:definition": "The official seal of the United States, adopted by the Confederation Congress on June 20, 1782, after three committees' work was combined by Charles Thomson: its front shows a bald eagle with an olive branch, thirteen arrows and the motto E pluribus unum, and its never-engraved reverse shows an unfinished pyramid under the Eye of Providence. The Secretary of State has kept it since 1789.",
