   },
   "skos:definition": "The Haudenosaunee (\"People of the Longhouse\") are a confederacy of six Native nations — the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga, Seneca and Tuscarora — united under the Great Law of Peace, whose Grand Council still meets at Onondaga in central New York and whose treaties with the United States, including the 1794 Treaty of Canandaigua, the nations regard as binding today.",
