   "skos:definition": "A federally funded scientific expedition led by geologist Ferdinand V. Hayden from June to October 1871 that mapped, measured, sketched and photographed the Yellowstone region; its reports, specimens, maps and images, including William Henry Jackson's photographs and Thomas Moran's art, fed the campaign that produced the Yellowstone National Park Act of March 1, 1872.",
