   "skos:definition": "A 726-foot concrete arch-gravity dam in Black Canyon of the Colorado River on the Arizona–Nevada border, built by the Six Companies consortium for the Bureau of Reclamation between 1931 and 1936; it created Lake Mead, supplies water and hydroelectric power across the Southwest, and was known officially as Boulder Dam from 1933 until Congress restored Herbert Hoover's name in 1947.",
