   "skos:definition": "A Virginia lawyer, Revolutionary War officer, congressman and secretary of state (1755–1835) who served as Chief Justice of the United States from 1801 to 1835, the longest tenure in that office, and whose opinions established judicial review and a broad view of national power, while he also enslaved hundreds of people over his lifetime and wrote the foundational decisions of federal Indian law.",
