   },
   "skos:definition": "The power of American courts, above all the Supreme Court, to decide whether a law or other government act conflicts with the Constitution and to refuse to enforce it if it does; the Constitution does not state the power expressly, but the Supreme Court first used it against an act of Congress in Marbury v. Madison (1803).",
