   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "us:labor-history-of-the-united-states"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The killing of at least nineteen unarmed striking coal miners, nearly all Polish, Slovak and Lithuanian immigrants, by a Luzerne County sheriff's posse on the road to Lattimer, Pennsylvania, on September 10, 1897; the sheriff and his deputies were acquitted, and the killings drove thousands of anthracite miners into the United Mine Workers.",
