   "skos:definition": "The domestic anticommunist campaign of the early Cold War, roughly 1947 to 1957, in which federal loyalty programs, congressional investigations, blacklists and laws aimed at the Communist Party cost thousands of Americans their jobs; it is named after Senator Joseph McCarthy of Wisconsin, whose reckless accusations from 1950 to 1954 made him its most visible figure.",
