    "@value": "1820-03-06"
   },
   "skos:altLabel": [
    "36°30′ line",
    "Compromise of 1820",
    "Missouri Compromise of 1820",
    "Missouri Enabling Act of 1820",
    "Thomas Amendment",
    "Thomas Proviso"
   ],
   "skos:broader": [
    {
     "@id": "us:sectionalism"
    },
    {
     "@id": "us:territorial-expansion-of-the-united-states"
    }
   ],
   "skos:definition": "The 1820 act of Congress, signed by President James Monroe on March 6, 1820, that let Missouri enter the Union without a ban on slavery, paired its admission with that of Maine as a free state, and prohibited slavery in the rest of the Louisiana Purchase north of latitude 36°30′.",
   "skos:inScheme": {
