   "skos:definition": "The extension of the Monroe Doctrine that President Theodore Roosevelt announced in his annual message to Congress on December 6, 1904, claiming for the United States a right to intervene in Latin American and Caribbean nations that failed to keep order or pay foreign creditors, so that European powers would have no pretext to intervene themselves; it was officially abandoned in 1934.",
