    }
   ],
   "skos:definition": "The federal law, signed by President Franklin D. Roosevelt on June 22, 1944, that gave World War II veterans tuition and living allowances for school and training, federal guarantees on home, farm and business loans, and up to a year of unemployment pay; it reshaped postwar higher education and homeownership, but discrimination in how it was carried out left many Black and other veterans with far less.",
