   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "us:womens-suffrage-movement"
   },
   "skos:definition": "A Quaker-raised reformer (1820–1906) from Massachusetts and Rochester, New York, who worked for temperance and abolition, co-led the National Woman Suffrage Association with Elizabeth Cady Stanton, was convicted in 1873 of voting illegally, and campaigned for a federal woman suffrage amendment that was ratified fourteen years after her death as the Nineteenth Amendment.",
   "skos:inScheme": {
