   },
   "skos:definition": "A national holiday of the United States, observed on the fourth Thursday of November, that grew out of colonial and presidential days of thanksgiving, became an annual national observance with Abraham Lincoln's 1863 proclamation, and was fixed in federal law in 1941; its popular link to the 1621 Plymouth harvest gathering is remembered very differently by many Native people.",
