   },
   "skos:definition": "The forty-fourth U.S. state (admitted July 10, 1890), a high, dry Rocky Mountain and Great Plains state crossed by the Continental Divide; homeland of the Shoshone, Arapaho, Lakota, Cheyenne and other nations, it became in 1869 the first U.S. territory or state to grant women the vote, and in the 2020 census it was the least populous state.",
